**Decision**

Propose a small section-scoped JavaScript patch plus unique section-scoped form control IDs in Liquid. Do not change cart route, translations, variant availability handling, merchant settings, product data, or live theme state.

This is a proposed local patch only. Uploading/publishing is not authorized.

**Observed Facts**

- Two `compact-buy` sections can appear on one product template.
- Changing the second selector does not update that form’s submitted hidden variant ID.
- After replacing the first section in Theme Editor, its selector no longer updates its hidden input.
- Current JS uses `document.querySelector`, so it binds only the first `[data-variant-select]` and first `[data-cart-variant]`.
- Current JS only runs on `DOMContentLoaded`.
- Current Liquid repeats `id="VariantSelect"` across section instances.

**Source-Level Diagnosis**

There are two related bugs:

1. Multi-instance bug: `querySelector` selects only the first matching selector and hidden input in the document. With two sections, only the first select/input pair is wired. The second section’s visible selector can change while its own hidden `name="id"` input remains unchanged.

2. Theme Editor replacement bug: the binding occurs only on `DOMContentLoaded`. If Shopify’s Theme Editor replaces a section after initial load, the new DOM is inserted after the listener has already run, so the replacement section has no change handler.

There is also an accessibility/HTML correctness issue: every instance uses `id="VariantSelect"` and `for="VariantSelect"`, creating duplicate IDs when multiple sections exist.

**Smallest Compatible Patch**

`sections/compact-buy.liquid`

```liquid
<div data-product-picker data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <form action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post">
    <label for="VariantSelect-{{ section.id }}">
      {{ 'products.product.product_variants' | t }}
    </label>

    <select id="VariantSelect-{{ section.id }}" data-variant-select>
      {% for variant in product.variants %}
        <option
          value="{{ variant.id }}"
          {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
          {% if variant == product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}selected{% endif %}
        >
          {{ variant.title | escape }}
        </option>
      {% endfor %}
    </select>

    <input
      type="hidden"
      name="id"
      data-cart-variant
      value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
    >

    <button type="submit">
      {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
    </button>
  </form>
</div>
```

`assets/compact-buy.js`

```js
(() => {
  const SECTION_SELECTOR = '[data-product-picker]';

  function bindCompactBuySection(section) {
    if (!section || section.dataset.compactBuyBound === 'true') return;

    const selector = section.querySelector('[data-variant-select]');
    const variantInput = section.querySelector('[data-cart-variant]');

    if (!selector || !variantInput) return;

    selector.addEventListener('change', () => {
      variantInput.value = selector.value;
    });

    section.dataset.compactBuyBound = 'true';
  }

  function bindCompactBuySections(root = document) {
    if (root.matches && root.matches(SECTION_SELECTOR)) {
      bindCompactBuySection(root);
    }

    root.querySelectorAll(SECTION_SELECTOR).forEach(bindCompactBuySection);
  }

  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    bindCompactBuySections();
  });

  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', (event) => {
    bindCompactBuySections(event.target);
  });
})();
```

**Why This Patch Is Minimal**

- Keeps the existing form submission model: `POST` to `{{ routes.cart_add_url }}` with hidden `name="id"`.
- Keeps the existing translation keys.
- Keeps existing variant availability behavior: unavailable variants remain disabled in the selector.
- Does not alter product selection logic or cart behavior.
- Does not add new dependencies.
- Scopes each select/input lookup to its own `[data-product-picker]` section.
- Adds a Shopify Theme Editor section-load hook without requiring knowledge of broader theme conventions.
- Uses a simple bound flag to avoid duplicate listeners if initialization runs more than once.

**Preservation Requirements**

- Preserve the standard Shopify cart add route.
- Preserve `products.product.product_variants` and `products.product.add_to_cart` translations.
- Preserve variant IDs as option values.
- Preserve disabled options for unavailable variants.
- Preserve `product.selected_or_first_available_variant` as the initial hidden input value.
- Preserve unrelated `settings_data.json` merchant changes.
- Do not upload or publish to live theme `77100`.
- Limit any proposed work to unpublished preview theme `77102` / branch `fix/picker-review` if later authorized.

**Recommended Tests**

1. Multi-section behavior:
   - Render two `compact-buy` sections on one product template.
   - Change the first selector and verify only the first form’s hidden `name="id"` changes.
   - Change the second selector and verify only the second form’s hidden `name="id"` changes.

2. Theme Editor replacement:
   - Replace or reload a section in the Theme Editor.
   - Change the newly inserted selector.
   - Verify its hidden variant input updates.

3. Regression smoke:
   - Initial selected option still matches `product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id`.
   - Add-to-cart still submits the selected variant ID.
   - Unavailable variants remain disabled.

4. Markup:
   - With two section instances, verify select IDs are unique.
   - Verify each label’s `for` points to the select in the same section.

**Uncertainties**

- Unknown how `assets/compact-buy.js` is loaded.
- Unknown whether the theme already has section lifecycle utilities that should be used instead.
- Unknown behavior for all-unavailable products.
- Unknown subscription or selling-plan behavior.
- No Shopify rendering, browser execution, or Theme Editor session is available from the supplied evidence.

**Deployment State**

Draft patch only. Not applied, uploaded, saved, published, or verified in Shopify. Live theme `77100` is unchanged. Unpublished preview theme `77102` is the apparent target only after explicit authorization.

